{"availability":"available","full":"JCinnamon/image-colour-analyzer","name":"image-colour-analyzer","description":"Web tool for analyzing colour properties in large image datasets","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2024-08-21T04:14:31Z","updated":"2026-08-25T03:53:00Z","branch":"main","homepage":"http://www.jonathancinnamon.com/image-colour-analyzer/","topics":[],"demo":"https://www.jonathancinnamon.com/image-colour-analyzer/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:33.793Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:33.793Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:33.793Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:38:33.793Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A browser-based tool for measuring colour across a whole set of images at once. It clusters each image into its dominant colours, reports colour values in HSV, CIELAB and LCH, computes a suite of whole-image and spatial metrics, reads EXIF (including GPS), and exports everything as CSV. It handles ordinary flat photos as well as 360° / wide-angle imagery (equirectangular, fisheye, and azimuthal / tiny-planet projections), with solid-angle weighting, projection conversion, and polar spatial analysis. The tool is subject-agnostic — axes are labelled generically in degrees, so it is not specific…","Part of Vis-O-Matic, alongside Image Cutter and Image Visualizer."],"features":["Batch colour analysis — drop in a folder or a list of URLs; each image is downsampled to an analysis resolution you set, then measured locally.","K-means clustering — k-means++ initialisation with a fixed seed for reproducibility; 2–20 dominant colours per image, each reported in HSV, CIELAB and LCH with its pixel share.","Three levels of granularity — cluster-level, image-level, and optional pixel-level tables, plus a hue histogram.","EXIF passthrough — GPS, capture date, camera and orientation read from JPEGs and from PNGs carrying an eXIf chunk, including cut-outs exported by Image Cutter with GPS/EXIF preserved.","Transparency handling — composite transparent areas onto white, black or grey, or analyse opaque pixels only."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JCinnamon/image-colour-analyzer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"762c33c276ec087ccf8af34ad4845431b1c3a5f4c3140e11416a6ca9c7f1d155","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:33.998Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:33.998Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A browser-based tool for measuring colour across a whole set of images at once. It clusters each image into its dominant colours, reports colour values in HSV, CIELAB and LCH, computes a suite of whole-image and spatial metrics, reads EXIF (including GPS), and exports everything as CSV. It handles ordinary flat photos as well as 360° / wide-angle imagery (equirectangular, fisheye, and azimuthal / tiny-planet projections), with solid-angle weighting, projection conversion, and polar spatial analysis. The tool is subject-agnostic — axes are labelled generically in degrees, so it is not specific…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JCinnamon/image-colour-analyzer/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"Open the tool in a browser — no installation, no account, no server.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JCinnamon/image-colour-analyzer/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"There is no server, no account and no upload step.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JCinnamon/image-colour-analyzer/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"762c33c276ec087ccf8af34ad4845431b1c3a5f4c3140e11416a6ca9c7f1d155","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JCinnamon/image-colour-analyzer/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:33.999Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-25T03:53:00Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JCinnamon/image-colour-analyzer/blob/main/README.md"